# Shell scripts run on the user's machine and must keep LF line endings even
# in a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true; with CRLF, sh stops on the
# first line ("set: Illegal option -"). scripts/make_release.py also pins
# line-ending conversion off when it builds the release tarball.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Package data shipped gzipped (edmars/data): bytes, never text.
*.gz binary
